Stage: QA

Purpose:
  Quality Assurance stage. Owns testing and quality validation of the
  unit of work as a whole — functional correctness, regressions, edge
  cases — everything DO needs already validated before it deploys the
  result anywhere.


Requires:
  BE, API, and whichever of FE/MD are part of this unit of work (see
  chains.sdd -> MobileExample — QA always follows the full set of
  implementation stages that actually ran, not a fixed list).


Produces:
  Validated, tested unit of work, ready for deployment.


Blocks:
  DO — DO MUST NOT deploy a unit of work that has not passed QA (see
  chains.sdd -> Rules [C5]).


ReviewFailure:
  A QA failure reopens the responsible implementation stage, not just
  QA itself (see chains.sdd -> ReviewFailure, Rules [C13]).


Optional:
  QA is not optional for any unit of work that reaches implementation
  — see chains.sdd -> Completion, which requires all required reviews
  to have passed.


Skills:
  @../../skills/qa/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW testing is actually implemented belongs to skills/qa/, not
  here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/qa/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the QA responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes a QA step.
